{"issues":[{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"11489","self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/11489","key":"MC-134573","renderedFields":{"summary":null,"issuetype":null,"watches":null,"customfield_10070":null,"customfield_10061":"","created":"22/Jul/18 8:45 AM","customfield_10050":"","customfield_10051":null,"description":"<p>Hi. Whenever I optimize a large world Minecraft will freeze for me while doing the necessary backup.</p>\n<h3><a name=\"StepstoReproduce%3A\"></a><b>Steps to Reproduce:</b></h3>\n<ol>\n\t<li>Click on Optimize World (1.12 world)</li>\n\t<li>Click 'Backup and Load'</li>\n\t<li>See how Minecraft will freeze after a while.</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<p><b>OR:</b></p>\n<ol>\n\t<li>Click on Edit World</li>\n\t<li>Click 'Make Backup'</li>\n\t<li>See how Minecraft will freeze after a while.</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>For the test purpose I used the&nbsp;Białowieża Forest map showcased on Minecraft.net some time ago. This world is about 18GB large (~8GB bigger than our average server worlds). It will however finish doing the backup after a while and then start to run the chunk upgrade process which runs smoothly again.</p>\n\n<p>I've also uploaded a picture showcasing the problem. Yeah, my CPU is at 99%, but Minecraft had two full threads and about 10% of my CPU for this task so this shouldn't be a problem (while the OS drive and the drive Minecraft is installed on had also little work to do). The problem here seems to be (<em>just guessing</em>) that the <b>backup process is being done in the same thread as the render thread</b> instead of a worker thread.</p>","customfield_10054":null,"fixVersions":null,"customfield_10055":null,"resolution":null,"customfield_10047":"24/Aug/18 3:24 PM","customfield_10048":null,"labels":null,"customfield_10049":null,"attachment":[{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/13740","id":"13740","filename":"image-2018-07-22-17-3